# Product Module Routing — classify the task first

Before starting ANY development task, classify it into exactly **one** active
product modules, then use that module's branch + skill + workflow. Authority:
`docs/adr/0013-branch-sync-governance.md` §D1/§D2; mirrored in `CLAUDE.md`
§"Product module map & task routing" and `AGENTS.md` §3. Full per-module
navigation (开发目标 / 绑定 skill / prompt 模板 / 开发 workflow / 进入下一模块的触发条件 /
影响的模块) lives in **`docs/PRODUCT_MODULE_MAP.md`** and the dev-dashboard 产品结构图.

| 模块 | key | Surface | 主 / 短分支 | 任务归属信号 | 状态 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Web 版本 | `web` | `apps/web/`, `packages/xai-web-*`, `plugin-web-*` | `web` / `codex/web/<feature>` | Web 页面·组件、Vite SPA、浏览器持久化、共享 UI、`/app/*` | P0 active |
| 手机版 / 原生薄壳 | `mobile` | `apps/mobile/` + `apps/web` PWA/mobile metadata | mobile self-test lane / `codex/mobile/<feature>` | iPhone、Android、Capacitor、PWA installability、mobile WebView、安全区、触控布局 | operator-unfrozen self-test |
| Mac 桌面版 App | `app` | `apps/desktop/` (Tauri 2 Web container shell) | `desktop-next`→`dev` / `codex/desktop/<feature>` | Web SPA 主窗口、native chrome、菜单栏/托盘、离线、账号+Keychain、自动更新、通知、深链、host command implementation | P1 active |
| 桌面整理插件 / Widget | `plugin` | `apps/desktop/` 插件平台运行时 + `packages/plugin-*` | `desktop-plugin-next` / `codex/plugin/<feature>` | 插件 SDK、widget host、多窗口/overlay/click-through/grid persistence、桌面整理、快速入口、单插件 | G1 runtime active · packages P2 paused |
| 账号云同步层 | `sync` | sync-v1 stack + server | (paused) / `codex/sync/<feature>` | `syncScope`、push/pull、冲突、跨设备、账号云 | P2 paused |
| 官方网页 | `site` | Cloudflare deploy infra | (proposed) / `codex/site/<feature>` | 下载页、自动更新、release notes、营销 | PROPOSED |
| Admin / 控制面 | `admin` | prototype `docs/prototypes/admin-dashboard/` + roadmap manifest | `codex/admin/<feature>` | AI 配置、权限、用量、审计、运营后台 | ACTIVE roadmap-gated |

Hard rules (do not violate):

- `web → app` only flows through the D3 gate (`xai-web-to-desktop-sync`, W0–W4 +
  parity receipt). Never merge Web changes straight into `dev`.
- `mobile` is operator-unfrozen for rapid self-test MVP work only: start from
  `web`, reuse the Web build via PWA + Capacitor, and do not route mobile work
  through `dev` / Mac App unless a Mac-specific delta is explicitly required.
- Physical host location is not product ownership: Tauri/native-window commands live
  in the host process, but desktop multi-window / overlay / widget runtime is a
  `plugin` product concern. The `app` module is the Mac shell / Web container plus
  native chrome, not the desktop organizer.
- G1 plugin platform-runtime work (multi-window engine, grid persistence,
  window-command) is the active gate. Concrete plugin packages
  (clipboard/widgets/pet/meditation) remain P2 paused until G1 ships.
- `sync` only moves `syncScope: account-sync` entities; `device-local` never goes
  to the cloud (ADR-0013 §D4).
- `site` remains PROPOSED (owner-deferred) — do not open new work branches or
  treat it as an active line without operator confirmation; use `xai-feature-brief`
  to normalize as a placeholder.
- `admin` was operator-activated on 2026-06-05 but remains roadmap-gated: use
  `codex/admin/<feature>` and `docs/workflow/roadmap/xai-admin-dashboard-system-integration.md`,
  beginning with `xai-admin-dashboard-shell`; do not bypass RBAC, audit, secret,
  deploy, or production-write gates.
- iPhone / Android native thin shell work is active only under the `mobile`
  self-test lane. Future iPad dedicated native / Apple Watch / browser-extension
  surfaces remain planning-only `future_surfaces`; never classify them as active
  module targets without operator confirmation.
- `desktop-next` / `desktop-plugin-next` / `release/desktop/<version>` are defined
  but **not yet created**; creating them (and anything touching `dev`) needs explicit
  operator confirmation.
- Same-Web-line deploy/CSP changes (`apps/web/wrangler.toml`, `apps/web/public/_headers`)
  follow the ADR-0008 extension protocol + feature-plan/review — NOT the D3 gate.

This routing rule is synced across `CLAUDE.md` §Product module map, `AGENTS.md` §3,
this file, and `docs/PRODUCT_MODULE_MAP.md`. Changing one means changing the others.
